# LangGraph conventions

- Every agent is a compiled `StateGraph`. No hand-rolled control flow that bypasses it.
- One node = one responsibility. A node that both generates and QC-scores is two nodes.
- The typed state schema is the *only* contract between nodes — no hidden shared mutable
  state, no reaching into another node's internals.
- Checkpoint after every node using the graph's checkpointer (Postgres-backed — see
  `docs/architecture/adr/0003-langgraph-checkpointing-strategy.md`). Never implement a
  parallel, ad-hoc "resume" mechanism.
- Conditional edges implement loop-with-cap patterns (e.g. QC pass/fail). The cap lives in
  state, evaluated by the edge condition — not as a scattered constant re-checked in
  multiple places.
- A node never calls a model provider or the Higgsfield client directly — only through the
  gateway alias (`02-model-routing.mdc`) or the provider abstraction
  (`14-provider-abstraction-mcp.mdc`).
- Node failures raise typed exceptions mapped to the platform error taxonomy — never a bare
  `Exception`. The exception type determines retry/fallback/circuit-break/degrade routing.
